# {{ package }}

{{ description }}

## Installation

```bash
php bin/neo neophp:package:install {{ package }}
```

The configuration is copied into `config/packages/{{ alias }}/`.

## Configuration

`config/packages/{{ alias }}/{{ alias }}.yaml` (key `packages.{{ alias }}.{{ alias }}`):

```yaml
greeting: Hello
```

| Option | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `greeting` | `Hello` | word used by `greet()` |

## Usage

Inject `{{ namespace }}\{{ class }}ManagerInterface` in a service, a command or a controller:

```php
use {{ namespace }}\{{ class }}ManagerInterface;

public function __construct(private {{ class }}ManagerInterface ${{ property }})
{
}
```

```php
$this->{{ property }}->greet('Neo');
```

Console:

```bash
php bin/neo {{ alias }}:hello Neo
```

Templates are rendered with the `@{{ alias }}` namespace and can be overridden in `templates/packages/{{ alias }}/` of the project:

```php
return $this->render('@{{ alias }}/hello', ['message' => $this->{{ property }}->greet('Neo')]);
```

## Disabling

In `config/config.php`:

```php
{{ namespace }}\{{ class }}Manager::class => false,
```

## Development

In a NeoPHP project, declare the directory of the package as a Composer path repository in `composer.json`:

```json
"repositories": [
    { "type": "path", "url": "{{ directory }}", "options": { "symlink": true } }
]
```

Then install it:

```bash
php bin/neo neophp:package:install {{ package }}:*@dev
```

